  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "The push source",
      "items": [
        "SNS keeps nothing, so the SQS subscription is what makes a past window re-readable",
        "The Receiver writes landing/ before deleting from the queue: a crash duplicates, never loses",
        "A Fetcher windows landing/ by publish time, dedupes on MessageId, one file per window"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Unchanged from phase 1",
      "items": [
        "Same Fetcher, Writer and window rules; only the medium moved from disk to S3",
        "Raw is still read in place as external tables; nothing is loaded",
        "Staging and marts are the same dbt models, but the repoint is an objective, not done: marts still hard-code a DuckDB materialisation and a local path"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "New in phase 2",
      "items": [
        "Mart builds commit through the DuckLake catalog on RDS, which is what should make concurrent dbt pods safe",
        "A Postgres-wire serving layer is the candidate front door; pg_duckdb does not list DuckLake as tested",
        "Auth, row-level security and audit are meant to come from Postgres roles; that is a spike, not a result"
      ]
    }
  ]
